# DMS Phase 1 — Driver Monitoring System

Production-oriented Phase 1 pipeline for verifying whether explainable facial measurements extracted via **MediaPipe Face Mesh** can explain FL3D driver state labels.

## Objective

Answer: **Can handcrafted physiological/geometric features explain driver state (alert / yawning / microsleep)?**

- FL3D provides **images + ground-truth labels only**
- FL3D landmark annotations are **ignored**
- All landmarks come from **MediaPipe Face Mesh (468+ points)**
- Classification is **rule-based** (no ML in Phase 1)

## Pipeline

```
FL3D Images → Dataset Loader → Face Detection → MediaPipe Face Mesh
    → Landmark Processing → Feature Extraction → Rule Engine
    → Evaluation vs FL3D Labels → Feature Dataset Export + EDA
```

## Project Structure

```
DMS Project/
├── configs/                 # YAML configuration
├── classification_frames/   # FL3D raw data (images + annotations)
├── data/features/           # Exported feature datasets
├── outputs/                 # Reports, figures, metrics
├── src/dms/                 # Source package
│   ├── dataset/             # FL3D loader (labels only)
│   ├── detectors/           # Modular face detection
│   ├── landmarks/           # MediaPipe Face Mesh
│   ├── features/            # EAR, MAR, head pose, gaze, quality
│   ├── rules/               # Rule-based classifier
│   ├── evaluation/          # Metrics + failure analysis
│   ├── analysis/            # EDA statistics
│   ├── visualization/       # Plots
│   └── pipeline/            # End-to-end orchestration
└── tests/
```

## Setup

```bash
cd "DMS Project"
python -m venv .venv
.venv\Scripts\activate        # Windows
pip install -r requirements.txt
pip install -e .
```

## Run Pipeline

**Full run** (all configured splits — may take hours on ~53k images):

```bash
python -m dms.pipeline --config configs/default.yaml
```

**Debug run** (10 samples per split):

```bash
python -m dms.pipeline --config configs/default.yaml --max-samples 10 --splits train
```

## Outputs

Each run creates `outputs/runs/<timestamp>/` containing:

| Artifact | Description |
|---|---|
| `config_snapshot.json` | Reproducible config |
| `validation_report.json` | Dataset integrity |
| `metrics/evaluation.json` | Accuracy, F1, confusion matrix |
| `reports/eda_summary.json` | Feature statistics |
| `reports/failure_analysis.json` | Misclassification analysis |
| `reports/misclassified.csv` | Failed samples |
| `figures/` | Histograms, scatter, box plots, correlation |

Feature datasets are exported to `data/features/features_<timestamp>.csv` and `.parquet`.

## Configuration

Edit `configs/default.yaml` to adjust:

- Data paths and splits
- Detector provider (`mediapipe` / `retinaface`)
- MediaPipe confidence thresholds
- Rule thresholds (`mar_yawning`, `ear_microsleep`)
- Enabled feature groups

Landmark indices: `configs/landmarks_mediapipe.yaml`

## Tests

```bash
pytest tests/ -v
```

## Phase 2 Compatibility

Feature extraction is **dataset-independent**. Future pipeline:

```
Video → Frames → Face Detection → Face Mesh → Features → Temporal Model → Alert
```

Only the dataset loader and frame source change; detectors, landmarks, and features remain unchanged.

## Feature Vector (exported columns)

| Category | Features |
|---|---|
| Eye | `ear_left`, `ear_right`, `ear_avg`, `eye_opening`, `eyes_closed`, `blink_proxy` |
| Mouth | `mar`, `mouth_opening`, `mouth_width_norm`, `yawning_indicator` |
| Head | `pitch`, `yaw`, `roll` |
| Gaze | `gaze_horizontal`, `gaze_vertical`, `gaze_magnitude` |
| Quality | `blur`, `brightness`, `detection_confidence` |
| Geometric | `eye_distance`, `face_height_ratio`, `symmetry_score`, ... |

Plus: `ground_truth_label`, `predicted_label`, `subject_id`, `image_id`.
